{"id":"sako-trg","slug":"sako-trg","name":"Sako TRG","aliases":["TRG-42","TRG-22","TRG 42","TRG 22","TRG-21","TRG-41","Sako M995","Sako TRG-S","Sako TRG-42","Sako TRG-21","Sako TRG-22","Sako TRG-41","Sako TRG M10"],"kind":"firearm","category":"sniper-rifles","subcategory":"Sniper rifle","description":"The Sako TRG is a bolt-action sniper rifle line designed and manufactured by Finnish firearms manufacturer SAKO of Riihimäki. It is the successor to the SAKO TR-6 target rifle, and thus the letter G within the rifle's name is meant to represent number 7.","history":"Even though the TRG-21 obtained its origins from the successful Sako TR-6 target rifle and 1984–1986 development work for the hardly produced Valmet Sniper M86 rifle by the former Finnish state firearms company Valmet which merged with Sako, the 4.7 kg (10 lb 6 oz) TRG-21 was designed as a result of a thorough study of sniper requirements.","development":"The TRG system is almost unique in being a purpose-designed sniper rifle, rather than an accurised version of an existing, general-purpose rifle. The sniper rifles can have a matte or manganese phosphatised finish.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Cartridge & Action","items":[{"label":"Cartridge","value":".260 Remington"},{"label":"Cartridge","value":"(TRG-22)"},{"label":"Cartridge","value":"6.5mm Creedmoor","numeric":6.5,"unit":"mm"},{"label":"Cartridge","value":"(TRG-22 A1)"},{"label":"Action","value":"Bolt-action"},{"label":"Feed System","value":"5-round detachable box magazine (.338 Lapua Magnum)"},{"label":"Feed System","value":"7-round detachable box magazine (.300 Winchester Magnum and .375 CheyTac)"},{"label":"Feed System","value":"10-round detachable box magazine (.308 Winchester)"},{"label":"Sights","value":"Aperture rear (with flip-up open tritium night/combat sight); day or night optics"}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Weight","value":"4.7 kg empty (TRG-22 black)","numeric":4.7,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Weight","value":"4.9 kg e